---
title: "oracle price refresh (Current Finance: XOracle)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_load_feed: load PythFeedData for coin_type
    q_load_feed --> q_verify_object: assert_pyth_price_info_object matches registered
    q_verify_object --> q_get_price: get_pyth_price(price_info_object, feed_data, clock)
    q_get_price --> q_extract: extract (ema, spot) from Pyth price feed
    q_extract --> q_check_base: base_token == USD?
    q_check_base --> q_update: update_price_feed(x_oracle, usd, coin_type, spot, ema)
    q_update --> q_store: prices[base_token][coin_type] = PriceFeed(spot, ema)
    q_store --> [*]

    note right of q_verify_object
        INV-001: Each coin_type has exactly one registered PriceInfoObject
        INV-002: Price has delay tolerance (default 5s, max 1800s)
        INV-003: EMA and spot prices tracked separately
        INV-004: Price queries can use EMA, spot, or both with tolerance check
        INV-005: Currently only USD base token supported
    end note
